@nsobid-F19B2E01E1794F933A9720C1404BB6F6

# Bayonetta 2 1.2 - 1920x1080 resolution

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Renders at 1920x1080 instead of the stock 1280x720. The game uses the same
// size docked and handheld, so the mod holds in both modes.
//
// The engine has one display size (the NVN window textures and the backbuffer
// viewport) and one scene size, which is passed to the two startup functions
// that build every render target. Most targets are sized from those arguments,
// but the rest of the post-process chain is hardcoded: a full-size target,
// three half-size targets, nine quarter-size targets and two 800x450 views.
// All of them are scaled by the same ratio so every buffer keeps its stock
// proportion to the frame. Binding a target sets the viewport and scissor to
// that target's own size, so no draw code needs to change.
//
// Bayonetta 2 also builds a three-step horizontal dynamic-resolution ladder
// (1280, 1024 and 800 wide, all 720 tall) as views into the full-size targets.
// Nothing in retail selects another step, but all three are pinned to 1920 so
// the resolution cannot drop if one is ever selected.
//
// The 2D layer (HUD, menus, fades, vignette and screen filters) is authored
// in a fixed 1280x720 space and asks the engine for the display size to build
// its projection. That size is pinned to 1280x720 so 2D elements fill the
// screen; the few blits that need the real pixel size are redirected to new
// getters that return it.
//
// REQUIRES Ryujinx > System > DRAM Size set to 6 GiB or higher. Every render
// target, including the swap-chain textures, comes out of two fixed GPU pools
// (128 MB and 64 MB) carved from a 1536 MB "GRAPHIC" heap inside a 2913 MB
// root heap. Both pools are enlarged for the 1920x1080 targets, and each parent
// heap grows by exactly the same amount so its stock headroom is unchanged:
// 512 MB and 96 MB pools, 1952 MB GRAPHIC heap, 3329 MB root heap. The root
// heap is malloc'd from nn::os::SetMemoryHeapSize(all remaining memory) and
// so follows the emulator's DRAM setting.
//
// The render-target pool also reserves room for the [Shadow Resolution 4096]
// mod. This mod OWNS the pool and heap offsets below; do not duplicate them in
// another enabled mod.

@enabled
// Display size (NVN window textures and the backbuffer viewport).
0097B880 0887C0D2   // MOVZ X8,#1080,LSL#32 (was 720)
0097B884 08F080F2   // MOVK X8,#1920 (was 1280)
// Scene size handed to the two render-target builders.
0097B9FC 00F08052   // shadow/depth set width  (was 1280)
0097BA00 01878052   // shadow/depth set height (was 720)
0097BA0C 00F08052   // main set width  (was 1280)
0097BA10 01878052   // main set height (was 720)
// Full-size target that the dynamic-resolution views alias.
0097D29C 19F08052   // width  (was 1280)
0097D2A4 02878052   // height (was 720)
// Half-size targets (640x360 at stock).
0097D2D0 01788052   // width  (was 640)
0097D2D4 82438052   // height (was 360)
0097D2FC 01788052   // width  (was 640)
0097D300 82438052   // height (was 360)
0097D328 01788052   // width  (was 640)
0097D32C 82438052   // height (was 360)
// Quarter-size post-process chain (320x180 at stock).
0097D354 013C8052   // width  (was 320)
0097D358 C2218052   // height (was 180)
0097D380 013C8052   // width  (was 320)
0097D384 C2218052   // height (was 180)
0097D3A8 013C8052   // width  (was 320)
0097D3AC C2218052   // height (was 180)
0097D3D0 013C8052   // width  (was 320)
0097D3D4 C2218052   // height (was 180)
0097D3F8 013C8052   // width  (was 320)
0097D3FC C2218052   // height (was 180)
0097D420 013C8052   // width  (was 320)
0097D424 C2218052   // height (was 180)
0097D448 013C8052   // width  (was 320)
0097D44C C2218052   // height (was 180)
0097D498 013C8052   // width  (was 320)
0097D49C C2218052   // height (was 180)
0097D4C0 013C8052   // width  (was 320)
0097D4C4 C2218052   // height (was 180)
// 800x450 views (0.625 of the frame).
0097DA8C 02968052   // width  (was 800)
0097DA98 63548052   // height (was 450)
0097DAC4 02968052   // width  (was 800)
0097DAC8 63548052   // height (was 450)
// Dynamic-resolution ladder widths, steps 1 and 2 (step 0 is the
// full-size width above).
0097DBA4 08F08052   // step 1 width (was 1024)
0097DBB0 09F08052   // step 2 width (was 800)
// Render-target memory pool, was 128 MB: alloc, pool size, allocator size.
00DC21F4 0100A452   // 512 MB
00DC2204 1600A452   // 512 MB
00DC2234 0700A452   // 512 MB
// Image-target memory pool, was 64 MB: alloc, pool size, allocator size.
00DC20BC 01C0A052   // 96 MB
00DC20CC 16C0A052   // 96 MB
00DC211C 07C0A052   // 96 MB
// GRAPHIC heap that both pools are carved from, was 1536 MB.
0096B340 0140AF52   // 1952 MB
// ALL RESOURCE root heap around it, was 2913 MB.
0096B008 0002BA52   // 3329 MB
// 2D canvas. The display-size getters are the 2D layer's coordinate space:
// UI projections, full-screen overlays and screen-space UVs all divide by
// them while their geometry is authored in 1280x720 units. Pin both getters
// to 1280x720 so the 2D layer stretches across the real display.
00DC4F34 00A08052   // canvas width:  MOVZ W0,#1280 (was LDR W0,[X8])
00DC4F44 005A8052   // canvas height: MOVZ W0,#720  (was LDR W0,[X8])
// Real display-size getters for the few callers that measure pixels, placed
// over _fini, which the game never calls (process exit only).
00000160 08A80190   // ADRP X8, display size page
00000164 006149B9   // LDR  W0,[X8,#0x960] = real width
00000168 C0035FD6   // RET
0000016C 08A80190   // ADRP X8, display size page
00000170 006549B9   // LDR  W0,[X8,#0x964] = real height
00000174 C0035FD6   // RET
// Pixel users: backbuffer size cache, full-screen blits scaled against the
// bound target, and the target-equals-screen test before a copy.
00976D20 1025DA97   // BL real width  (frame start, target size cache)
00976D28 1125DA97   // BL real height
0097722C CD23DA97   // BL real width  (final blit)
00977234 CE23DA97   // BL real height
00977380 7823DA97   // BL real width  (post blits)
00977388 7923DA97   // BL real height
00979ED0 A418DA97   // BL real width  (composite)
00979ED8 A518DA97   // BL real height
00EB41E4 DF2FC597   // BL real width  (screen copy test)
00EB41EC E02FC597   // BL real height
@stop

// Offsets reverse-engineered against Bayonetta 2 1.2 (PlatinumGames "Hw"
// framework, PRJ_010, NVN). The retail build is symbol-stripped; every site was
// located by structure and byte-verified against the IDB before being written.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-patches
